<http://data.silknow.org/object/159fe58f-a143-3c6f-a780-32aa91faac4d/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Two panels which, when joined down the centre, form a square cover. Linen embroidered with silk in regular surface darning.\nEach panel contains two vertical parallel stems which are formed by green outlines and red scale-like segments. A elicate green stem and leaf hangs down from the main stem and is attached to a large, segmented and pointed fruit.  This has not been identified but resembles a bunch of grapes.  This fruit forms three rows in which it alternates to the left and to the right.  Along each row a redfruit alternates with a blue fruit.\nEach panel has a border along three sides.  The border is divided into a series of niches formed by a blue line and each niche contains either a blue flower with a white centre or a red flower with a green centre."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/159fe58f-a143-3c6f-a780-32aa91faac4d> .

